  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ | $\\,0.4090\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ | $\\,0.4483\\,$ |\n\nThe data above is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>0.33).$ Use the table above and do not round your answer.\n\n$P(Z>0.33)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/597125714057269b7adf9c0a2a9bbdde9631cf37bc80518281ab4444c3189717.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=\u03a6(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>0.33).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/98cc48cff914158a4c8facf34de162a237e07ba271067aa51ba719a66f17d8af.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<-0.33).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/357a942bf0b8976c29eedb7f865c381a46c3f841eadfc2203ca3192cea8275af.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>0.33)=P(Z<-0.33)=\u03a6(-0.33)=0.3707.\n$$",
